  "releaseNotes": "# AID v2.1.2\n\n## 中文更新说明\n\n### 优化\n\n- 模型批量绑定模型池时，可为每个新增关系选择业务能力和默认能力；唯一能力或唯一模型默认能力会自动选中，已有业务绑定、SKU、价格、倍率和启停状态保持不变。\n- 模型池关系快照会忽略已删除、不存在或类型不匹配的失效模型引用，后台不再展示不可操作的删除占位项，并提供失效引用数量提示。\n\n### 修复\n\n- 修复部分早期数据库缺少待审成片字段时，历史增量 SQL 在 `pending_video_url` 处中断的问题；新增结构归一迁移补齐当前程序必需的表、字段和索引。\n- 修复少数旧源码构建环境生成的升级器缺少清单验签公钥、无法先升级升级器的问题；签名清单与制品 SHA256 校验继续强制启用。\n- 修复脚本升级先替换程序、后执行数据库迁移造成的半升级状态；数据库迁移现在先于三端产物切换，失败时自动恢复完整数据库快照并重启原版本。\n- 修复历史迁移按文件名字典序执行、已成功脚本可能被重复执行或内容变化后静默重放的问题；迁移改为 SemVer 顺序和独立历史记录管理。\n- 修复新安装基线缺少图片内容安全审查日志表的问题。\n- 修复模型池清理迁移可能误处理非数组、损坏或超长历史配置的问题；无法安全自动解析的配置及其有效绑定保持原样，普通数组中的失效引用仍会被幂等清理。\n\n### 兼容性与升级说明\n\n- 升级前请备份数据库、部署配置、证书和用户媒体目录；升级执行可重复运行的 `sql/v2.1.2.sql`。\n- 已完成 MySQL 5.7.44 连续升级矩阵验证：`v1.0.0-beta.1` 至 `v2.1.1` 的 15 个可重建官方初始化基线均可升级至本版本，迁移重复执行后结构和公共基线保持稳定。\n- 本版本将正式渠道一键直升最低版本扩展至 `v1.0.0-beta.1`。早期环境允许保留不冲突的历史表和用户数据，不以删表方式强制追平表数量。\n- 本次 Web 用户端无功能变化；服务端和后台管理端需同步更新。\n\n## English Release Notes\n\n### Improved\n\n- Bulk model-to-pool binding now lets administrators choose business capabilities and the default capability for each new relation. A sole compatible capability or sole declared model default is selected automatically, while existing bindings, SKUs, prices, multipliers, and enablement states remain unchanged.\n- Model-pool snapshots now ignore deleted, missing, or type-incompatible model references. The admin UI no longer exposes unusable deleted placeholders and reports the number of stale references.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed early databases failing historical migrations at `pending_video_url`; a new convergence migration supplies every currently required table, column, and index.\n- Fixed updater binaries built by some early source environments missing the embedded manifest-verification key. Signed-manifest and artifact SHA256 verification remain mandatory.\n- Fixed script upgrades replacing application artifacts before database migration. Migrations now run first; failures restore the complete database snapshot and restart the previous version.\n- Fixed lexicographic migration ordering and unsafe replay behavior. Migrations now follow SemVer order and use an auditable execution-history table.\n- Restored the image-content moderation log table in the fresh-install baseline.\n- Fixed the model-pool cleanup migration potentially modifying non-array, malformed, or oversized historical configuration. Configurations that cannot be safely normalized and their valid bindings are preserved, while stale references in normal arrays are still removed idempotently.\n\n### Compatibility and Upgrade Notes\n\n- Back up the database, deployment configuration, certificates, and user media before upgrading. The repeatable migration is `sql/v2.1.2.sql`.\n- The MySQL 5.7.44 continuous-upgrade matrix passed for all 15 reconstructable official baselines from `v1.0.0-beta.1` through `v2.1.1`, including a second complete migration pass.\n- The stable-channel one-click upgrade floor is extended to `v1.0.0-beta.1`. Non-conflicting legacy tables and user data are intentionally preserved instead of being deleted solely to match table counts.\n- The Web client has no functional changes in this release; update the server and admin application together.",
